","to me"],["אֱלֹהַי","'elohai","H430","HNcmpc/Sp1bs","O God my"],["לְטוֹבָה","letovah","H2896","HR/Ncfsa","for good"]],"x":[[16013014,16013014,8],[16013022,16013022,7],[19106004,19106004,5],[16010034,16010034,3],[19025007,19025007,3],[19026008,19026009,3]],"xn":6}},"people":[{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2]},{"id":"balaam_593","name":"Balaam","also":"","summary":"Lord of the people; foreigner or glutton, as interpreted by others, the son of Beor, was a man of some rank among the Midianites (Num. 31:8; comp. 16).","verses":59,"father":"Beor","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"tobiah_2872","name":"Tobiah","also":"","summary":"Pleasing to Jehovah, the “servant,” the “Ammonite,” who joined with those who opposed the rebuilding of Jerusalem after the Exile (Neh. 2:10).","verses":12,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4,7,8]},{"id":"eliashib_1101","name":"Eliashib","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4,7]},{"id":"artaxerxes_314","name":"Artaxerxes","also":"","summary":"The king mentioned in Ezra 7:1, in the seventh year (B.C. 458) of whose reign Ezra led a second colony of Jews back to Jerusalem, was probably Longimanus, who reigned for forty years (B.C. 464-425); the grandson of Darius, who, fourteen years later, permitted Nehemiah to return and rebuild Jerusalem.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"hanan_1377","name":"Hanan","also":"","summary":"The treasurer.","verses":1,"father":"Zaccur","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"mattaniah_1960","name":"Mattaniah","also":"","summary":"The gatekeeper.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"pedaiah_2298","name":"Pedaiah","also":"","summary":"A Levite in charge of the storerooms and was responsible for distributing supplies to fellow Levites.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"shelemiah_2597","name":"Shelemiah","also":"","summary":"God is my perfection; my happiness; my peace.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"zaccur_2968","name":"Zaccur","also":"","summary":"The son of Mattaniah (Neh. 13:13).","verses":1,"father":"Mattaniah","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"zadok_2979","name":"Zadok","also":"","summary":"“The scribe” set over the treasuries of the temple by Nehemiah along with a priest and a Levite (Neh. 13:13).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[23]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[26]},{"id":"sanballat_2470","name":"Sanballat","also":"","summary":"Held some place of authority in Samaria when Nehemiah went up to Jerusalem to rebuild its ruined walls. He vainly attempted to hinder this work (Neh. 2:10, 19; 4:1-12; 6).","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"eliashib_1100","name":"Eliashib","also":"","summary":"A high priest in the time of Ezra and Nehemiah (Neh. 12:22, 23). He rebuilt the eastern city wall (3:1), his own mansion being in that quarter, on the ridge Ophel (3:20, 21).","verses":4,"father":"Joiakim","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"joiada_1680","name":"Joiada","also":"","summary":"","verses":4,"father":"Eliashib","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"son_of_joiada_2768","name":"son of Joiada","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Joiada","mother":"","v":[28]}],"places":[{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[6]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[6,7,15,16,19,20]},{"id":"ammon_58","name":"Ammon","kind":"","lat":31.95522,"lon":35.94503,"summary":"The usual name of the descendants of Ammon, the son of Lot (Gen. 19:38). From the very beginning (Deut. 2:16-20) of their history till they are lost sight of (Judg. 5:2), this tribe is closely associated with the Moabites (Judg. 10:11; 2 Chr. 20:1; Zeph. 2:8).","verses":12,"v":[23]},{"id":"ashdod_101","name":"Ashdod","kind":"City","lat":31.75604,"lon":34.65606,"summary":"Stronghold, a Philistine city (Josh. 15:47), about midway between Gaza and Joppa, and 3 miles from the Mediterranean. It was one of the chief seats of the worship of Dagon (1 Sam. 5:5).","verses":19,"v":[23,24]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[23]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1931,1931,3117,5612,5612,4872,4872,7121,7121,7121,241,241,241,5971,5971,5971,0,0,0,4672,4672,3789,3789,3789,834,3808,5984,4125,4125,5704,5